Cyde Weys <vze23tnc@verizon.net> writes:

> This is my current wizard.  He has more than double the score of any 
> other wizard I've ever played.  Some notable things he's lacking: ID'ed 
> scrolls of genocide or charging, no Bag of Holding, no magic markers, 
> and no good armor.  

Unless you want to go polypileless, collect 
every magic tool and armor you come across.  
This includes 

- Elven cloaks
- Elven boots 
- Boots/Gauntlets of Fumbling/Kicking/Jumping

- Unicorn horns
- magic whistles 

Also, collect all scrolls/spellbooks/rings/wands.  Wait for 
a wand of polymorph to fall in your capable hands.  Arrange 
the stuff in a neat row of 3-4 piles, and take care to distribute 
all kinds evenly (a big pile of scrolls/spellbooks is not a 
good idea, and don't even think of piling up metal things), 
then give it a healthy polyzap.  Have a look, identify all new 
unknown items, choose what to keep and polyzap anew; maybe 
repeat this a third time as well.  This method usually yields 
one or two neat items, maybe more in the scroll department.  
(Divide up stacked scrolls like "14 scrolls of teleportation" 
to improve chances of getting something good.)  

> I'm thinking I should bless the magic lamp and use 
> it wish for a GDSM so I don't have to take off my dwarvish mithril 
> everytime to cast a spell.  

Good idea.  Much more important than this, IMHO,   
is the better AC.  Plus, you can switch your 
cloak.  (You might also be interested in keeping 
the cloak, wishing for SDSM and having the amulet 
slot free, but that's a matter of taste.)  Keep in 
mind to choose a cloak with a good magic cancellation 
factor, though.  

> of my equipment.  I found an athame in one of the bones piles when I 
> already had Magicbane (I thought there couldn't be duplicate artifacts?  
> Or was the other one no longer Magicbane?).  

Since it's not called Magicbane, I'd assume it is not 
Magicbane ;-).  Athames are 'normal' weapons, though rarely 
found (usually in the remainders of a lich).  Each artifact 
is a special version of a 'normal' weapon type; if you 
already have an artifact and stumble over a bones file 
witht the same artifact, the game replaces the second 
one with a corresponding 'normal' weapon.  

